      "original": "सुन्दर सुन्दर विनायक\nशुभ मंगल दायक विनायक\nविघ्न कोटि हर विमल गजानन\nसकल विघ्न हर साई गजानन\nईश्वरी नन्दन पार्थी गजानन",
      "transliteration": "Sundara Sundara Vinayaka\nShubha Mangala Dayaka Vinayaka\nVighna Koti Hara Vimala Gajanana\nSakala Vighna Hara Sai Gajanana\nEshwari Nandana Parthi Gajanana",
      "translation": "Victory to Lord Ganesha who is very beautiful, who bestows everything good and auspicious. He is the remover of millions of obstacles that come in our way. He is the elephant-faced son of Parvathi and is verily Lord Sai who resides in Parthi.",
